                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat H^1_{flat}(pt) = \hat H^1(pt) = \mathbb{R}/\mathbb{Z} = \hat K^1(pt)
          %p
            %strong Theorem (Hopkins-Singer)
          %p
            For each generalized cohomology theory
            %math#mathml_43c142bd26492806eb706aa0500abcb194dae6d7_45.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi E
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^*
            a differential version
            %math#mathml_43c142bd26492806eb706aa0500abcb194dae6d7_46.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat E^*
            as in the above definition does exist
          %p
            Moreover
            %math#mathml_43c142bd26492806eb706aa0500abcb194dae6d7_47.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
